{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":153847,"duration_api_ms":185352,"num_turns":8,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"a0e177ae-a604-4fc2-a85b-8c3df3650f9a","total_cost_usd":0.54106195,"usage":{"input_tokens":2724,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33709,"cache_read_input_tokens":201503,"output_tokens":5436,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33709,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":57,"outputTokens":7343,"cacheReadInputTokens":188922,"cacheCreationInputTokens":19556,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.08010919999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2724,"outputTokens":5436,"cacheReadInputTokens":201503,"cacheCreationInputTokens":33709,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.46095275,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Verified all six amendments against the current source code. Accepted three that identify real correctness/observability defects (density_factor unused in spawning, minerals missing from suppression diagnostics, stale chemistry confounding depth test). Rejected the commit structure suggestion (not a code defect), the redox water-change claim (no water changes exist in the test), and the biofilter 95% assertion claim (the code uses a 0.02g minimum threshold, not 95% comparison).","votes":[{"amendment_id":"fr-1-49d3b132","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified in source. `density_factor` is computed at line 714 via `density_repro_factor()` but never multiplied into `spawn_rate` (line 716-717: `base_spawn_rate * reproductive_readiness_index * f_mineral`). Density enters spawning only through the lagged EMA of `reproductive_readiness_index` (smoothing=0.1), meaning a sudden density spike takes many ticks to suppress spawning. Meanwhile `density_factor` is only used in the diagnostic event string, creating a misleading variable. This is a real correctness/observability defect."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-c4841f7b","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified in source. `reproductive_readiness_factors()` (lines 1438-1466) returns exactly 7 factors: temperature, condition, stability, molt_stress, density, tan, nitrite. `gh_mineral_factor` is absent. Since `dominant_repro_suppression_label()` (lines 1477-1489) finds the minimum of these 7 factors, it can never identify mineral deficiency as the dominant suppression — even when low GH is directly multiplying spawn_rate to near-zero via `f_mineral` (line 716) and hatch_rate (line 874). This breaks the observability contract for suppression diagnostics."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-f9a344a2","decision":"reject","rationale":"This is a commit-organization preference, not a concrete code defect. It identifies no correctness, safety, robustness, or maintainability issue in the code itself. Any real technical problems in the bundled file are properly captured by other amendments (fr-1-153ec732, fr-1-1d9eb769, etc.)."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-ef68088f","decision":"reject","rationale":"Verified: grep for `WaterChange|water_change|source_profile` in e2e_habitat_geometry_probes.rs returns zero matches. The redox probe (`probe_substrate_redox_denitrification`) uses `HarnessRun::from_state()` and steps hours in a simple loop (lines 815-818) without any water change actions. The claimed `UnknownSourceProfile` failure path does not exist in the current code."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-153ec732","decision":"reject","rationale":"The amendment's core factual claim is wrong. It states lines 246-259 'require the 2×-media run to finish with at least 95% of the small run's nitrifier biomass,' but the actual code at those lines uses a flat minimum threshold: `min_nitrifier_g = 0.02` with `assert!(bio_small > min_nitrifier_g && bio_large > min_nitrifier_g)`. There is no 95% comparison. The comment explicitly explains 'With the same bioload, the larger filter has lower nitrifier density (nutrient-limited, not area-limited), so we check that both achieve non-trivial biomass rather than comparing directly.' The described failure mode cannot occur with the current assertions."},{"amendment_id":"fr-1-1d9eb769","decision":"accept","rationale":"Verified in source. `TankState::new()` calls `WaterState::default_for_volume_l()` sizing ALL dissolved pools for the default geometry volume. The test then mutates fill_height (18 cm vs 55 cm), recalculates `volume_l`, and rescales only 5 pools (ammonia, nitrate, phosphate, DIC, DO) to the new volume. All other pools (alkalinity, Ca/Mg, chloride, DOC/DON, etc.) retain default-volume totals, producing different concentrations in shallow vs deep tanks. With very different fill heights on the same footprint, this is a significant confound that undermines the test's claim of isolating depth/light effects."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"56635e3b-27aa-42f2-b8e4-0cf2aac8f383"}
